{
  "id": null,
  "uid": "zcrypto-logs",
  "title": "Logs",
  "description": "Every log line the fleet ships, and the rate lane that says whether anything is arriving at all. Filter by machine, container, level and a substring. The capture daemon, the trading engine and the liquidations poller push one JSON object per record straight to the log store, so their lines are unpacked here at query time; lines collected from the systemd journal and from the shipping agent itself were unpacked when they were collected and pass through untouched. Every panel that serves an alert plots that alert's own expression and carries its own threshold line, so what you see here is the number the page was computed from.",
  "tags": [],
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 0,
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "liveNow": false,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 101,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Total lines/min",
      "description": "Is anything arriving at all? One line, every selected stream summed — the transport canary, and the panel a \"no lines in the last six hours\" page lands on. A flat zero here while the fleet is otherwise healthy means the shipping path is down, not that the fleet went quiet. Context panel: no alert evaluates this expression, so it carries no threshold line — the silence rules and the exact count each of them computes are drawn on the by-machine panel to the right. Counted per minute; the shipping paths here are low-volume by design, so a healthy total is a small number.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-logs"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-logs"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate({host=~\"$host\", container=~\"$container\"}[5m])) * 60",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "all selected streams",
          "queryType": "range"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "cpm",
          "custom": {
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "off"
            }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "none"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 102,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Lines/min by level",
      "description": "Did the mix of levels shift? An error band appearing under a flat total is the signal a total-only view hides, and a leveled band collapsing while the grey total stays flat is the other one — that is a parser or labelling regression rather than a dead transport, and it sends you to a different layer, which is why the raw total is re-drawn here beside the leveled series. The three series on the right axis are the exact fifteen-minute counts the three error rules evaluate. Their bar sits at one line, not at zero: these are whole-line counts, so one line is the smallest value that fires. All three fire the moment they cross, with no pending period. The archive-pull series carries no machine filter because that container name exists only on the NAS — the ops machine's own pull loop ships under a different name.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-logs"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 0
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-logs"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (level) (rate({host=~\"$host\", container=~\"$container\", level=~\".+\"}[5m])) * 60",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{level}}",
          "queryType": "range"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-logs"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate({host=~\"$host\", container=~\"$container\"}[5m])) * 60",
          "refId": "B",
          "legendFormat": "all lines, leveled or not",
          "queryType": "range"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-logs"
          },
          "expr": "topk(5, sum by (host, container, level, msg) (count_over_time({host=~\"zcrypto|zcrypto-red\", container=\"capture\", level=~\"ERROR|CRITICAL\"} | json message=\"message\" | drop __error__, __error_details__ | label_format msg=`{{ if .message }}{{ printf \"%.200s\" .message }}{{ else }}{{ printf \"%.200s\" __line__ }}{{ end }}` [15m]))) or on() vector(0)",
          "refId": "C",
          "legendFormat": "error window · capture daemon {{msg}}",
          "queryType": "range",
          "step": "5m"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-logs"
          },
          "expr": "topk(5, sum by (host, container, level, msg) (count_over_time({host=\"ops\", container=~\"alloy|liquidations|zcrypto-.*\", level=~\"ERROR|CRITICAL\"} | json message=\"message\" | drop __error__, __error_details__ | label_format msg=`{{ if .message }}{{ printf \"%.200s\" .message }}{{ else }}{{ printf \"%.200s\" __line__ }}{{ end }}` [15m]))) or on() vector(0)",
          "refId": "D",
          "legendFormat": "error window · ops {{container}} {{msg}}",
          "queryType": "range",
          "step": "5m"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-logs"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (host) (count_over_time({container=\"archive-pull\", level=~\"ERROR|CRITICAL\"} [15m])) or on() vector(0)",
          "refId": "E",
          "legendFormat": "error window · archive-pull loop",
          "queryType": "range",
          "step": "5m"
        }
      ],
